Method and limits
Each simulated future draws a random yearly return for a 70/30 stock/bond mix (after
inflation: stocks average 5% with 16% volatility, bonds 2% with 6%), adds contributions
while working, and withdraws spending net of Social Security in retirement. It's built in
Python with NumPy, pandas and matplotlib, and the seed is fixed, so every result
reproduces.
Bell-curve returns understate crashes, and the model leaves out taxes, fees and spending
changes. Next I'd add 401(k) taxes, historical returns, a stock-to-bond glide path and
spending guardrails.
